AB  - 6G promises ubiquitous connectivity (e.g., integrated space-air-ground-underwater networks) and new services Internet of Everything (IoE), holographic and immersive applications such as Virtual Reality (VR) and Augmented Reality (AR), autonomous systems, and ultra-reliable low-latency communication, etc. To recognize the full potential of 6th generation (6G) networks (i.e., utilizing terahertz frequencies to achieve peak data rates in Tbps, massive device density (> 107 devices/km2), latency of 0.1 ms, near-100% reliability, and energy consumption of 1 pJ/bit [1]), new paradigms for network management are needed to handle vast amounts of data, optimize computation and energy resources, and ensure robust security measures across various applications and distributed devices. The synergy of AI and blockchain can enable reliable, secure, and autonomous management in 6G. The blockchain ensures a trusted platform and distributed control plane, while AI provides proactive network configuration, intelligent resource optimization, adaptive decision-making, and the creation of dedicated virtual networks tailored to specific applications. This chapter outlines the state of the art in AI and blockchain-enabled networks for 6G, highlights current research trends, discusses future directions, and outlines major challenges.
