AB  - The field of artificial intelligence (AI) is changing deeply and moving from simple reactivity to active autonomy, called Agentic AI. The analysis in this research paper covers the main ideas, main traits, and the various architectural designs of Agentic AI. It looks at how Agentic AI developed, explaining that it allows devices to make choices and act on their own in different conditions, which is far better than what earlier automation or generative AI could do. The paper looks into the different methods these systems use to learn and improve. Additionally, it evaluates Agentic AI and how it currently pleases customers, enhances healthcare, reduces risks in finance, supports manufacturing, ensures cybersecurity, and improves research. At the same time, the report discusses the major technical, ethical, and social issues linked to creating autonomous AI, including accountability, bias, and the problem of control. At the end, the paper calls for future work, underscoring the goal of an Agentic web and pointing out the importance of strictly governing how Agentic AI is developed and used.
