AB  - This chapter explores smart transportation and relevant intricate security challenges with edge artificial intelligence (AI) integration. Smart transportation systems signify a major breakthrough in the development of urban transit, embodying a shift towards more advanced, efficient, and sustainable methods in travel and logistics management. At the same time, Edge AI significantly enhances smart transportation systems by enabling effective data processing and timely decision-making, improving efficiency, safety, and sustainability in urban transit systems. However, the implementation of Edge AI also poses security challenges stemming from its inherently distributed nature. The threats can compromise data integrity and model accuracy, undermining decision-making processes. This study conducts a comprehensive examination of current applications of Edge AI in smart transportation systems, with a particular emphasis on associated security concerns. Additionally, this chapter highlights the importance of establishing standardized protocols across various Internet of Things (IoT) devices and systems to enhance security measures. It further discusses the essential roles of consistent software updates, robust physical security, and resilient network infrastructure in upholding the integrity of these systems. The study emphasizes the necessity of a positive strategy to safeguard IoT and edge computing to defend against the continuously evolving landscape of cyber threats, especially in the context of distributed learning environments deployed in complicated scenarios.
