AB  - In multi-criteria decision-making problems, decision-makers must evaluate data with multiple, often conflicting, attributes. The Skyline operator can effectively identify Pareto-optimal solutions and offer interpretable results. This paper presents a comprehensive review of Skyline-based approaches by classifying Skyline queries into eight categories: Traditional, Regional, Ranking-based, Transformation-based, Probabilistic, Spatio-Temporal, Representative, and Group Skylines. We further compare these Skyline categories and relate them to classical methods such as weighted scoring, top-k rankings, and AI/ML approaches, highlighting trade-offs in time complexity, application scenarios, scalability, interpretability, preference handling, robustness to noise, and evaluation metrics. Finally, we outline future directions, including blockchain integration, privacy-preserving computation, and hybrid AI-enhanced models, providing a concise reference and guidance for researchers and practitioners seeking to advance Skyline-based multi-criteria decision analysis.
