AB  - The interplay between artificial intelligence and data protection norms remains inherently complex, a reality further compounded by the introduction of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act. Recognising this, several bodies and authorities have issued multiple documents addressing the intersection of AI and data protection. Among them, the European Data Protection Board has provided Opinion 28/2024 on data protection in AI models, seeking to bring clarity to these issues. This paper aims to contextualise and critically analyse these Guidelines, interpreting them in light of contemporary developments in AI-related data protection.
